 # Neural Texture Decoder
+
 Also called: Neural Volume Decoder, Texture Decoder
 
 ## Overview
-The Neural Texture Decoder is a convolutional network module that generates a high-resolution volumetric texture field from a compact latent vector [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of mapping low-dimensional scene representations to dense 3D spatial data, enabling differentiable rendering from 3D shapes [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from its sibling [MLPRender_Fea](2414-mlprender-fea.md) by using a fully convolutional architecture to produce a 3D tensor output rather than a per-ray MLP prediction [S1, unofficial].
+The Neural Texture Decoder is a convolutional neural network that generates spatial neural texture stacks (NTS) or stylized feature maps from latent inputs, serving as the final synthesis step in neural texture-based rendering pipelines [S1, unofficial]. It differs from MLP-based decoders by operating on spatial grids to preserve local geometric coherence, making it suitable for generating high-resolution texture maps for UV unwrapping or style transfer [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [MLPRender_Fea](2414-mlprender-fea.md).
 
 ## How it works
+The decoder transforms a low-dimensional latent vector into a high-resolution 3D volumetric feature map using a fully-connected layer followed by a series of 3D convolutions.
+
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   Input: A 199-dimensional vector $v \in \mathbb{R}^{199}$ [S1, unofficial].
-*   Output: A 4-channel tensor $T \in \mathbb{R}^{64 \times 64 \times 64 \times 4}$ representing the volumetric texture [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Input:** A 199-dimensional vector $v \in \mathbb{R}^{199}$.
+*   **Output:** A 4-channel tensor $T \in \mathbb{R}^{64 \times 64 \times 64 \times 4}$.
 
